        DIGITAL REDUCES PRICES ON STARION PERSONAL COMPUTERS;
                OFFERS MICROSOFT HOME CD BONUS PACK;
                      SIGNS NEW RETAIL OUTLETS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 25, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced it has lowered prices as much as 20 percent on 
several models of its Starion personal computer line.  At the same 
time, the company said it is offering a Microsoft Bonus Pack of CD 
titles -- valued at $300 -- to purchasers of all Starion PC models.  
The company also announced it has signed agreements with a number of 
retail outlets.

The new price cuts are available on the following Starion PC models:
   
     Model             New Price            Old Price

     300i              $1,599               $1,999
     500i              $1,799               $2,199
     700i              $1,999               $2,499
     900i              $2,499               $2,699

     The Microsoft Bonus Pack of popular home CD titles being 
offered on all Starion PCs includes Microsoft Encarta '95; Microsoft 
Bookshelf '95 (including American Heritage Dictionary, Roget's 
Thesaurus, National ZipCode Directory, Columbia Dictionary of 
Quotes, Hammond World Atlas, People's Chronology, World Almanac, and 
Columbia Concise Encyclopedia); Microsoft Golf 1.0; Microsoft 
Explorapedia -- The World of Nature; Microsoft Home CD Sampler and 
Microsoft Entertainment Pack.  The Bonus Pack titles are redeemable 
via a card available from the retailers. The completed card and sales 
receipt must be returned to Digital within 30 days of purchase.  
Combined, the pre-loaded and Bonus Pack software provide the customer 
with more than a dozen software titles valued at over $1,100.

     "With the new price cuts in the Starion line, Digital is 
delivering the best price offerings in the PC retail market," said 
Rod Keller, director, U.S. Consumer Market Development.  "In 
addition, the Microsoft Bonus Pack gives Digital a significant 
differentiator in the market, expanding the appeal of the Starion PC 
from the small business user to the home PC consumer."

     All of Digital's Starion models are packed with standard 
features including 8MB RAM; 1MB video DRAM; 14.4 data/fax modem; 
built-in answering machine; a dual or quad CD-ROM drive; and 16-bit 
stereo sound.  In addition, Starion models come pre-loaded with 
several robust business applications, including MS-DOS; Microsoft 
Windows for Workgroups; Claris Works; Intel ProShare; CompuServe; 
Lotus ScreenCam; "Getting Started" interface; fax/audio/answering 
machine software; and 11 Million Businesses Phone Book (available on 
the Starion 500i, 700i and 900i models only).

     The Starion 300i, 500i, 700i and 900i models are offered 
through CompUSA, Incredible Universe, and Nobody Beats the Wiz. The 
Microsoft Bonus Pack offer is available immediately.

     All Starion models carry a limited three-year warranty, with 
first year on-site.  Included with the systems is an upgrade coupon 
for Digital's Service-in-a-Box program.  Priced at $144, the program 
provides one year of telephone support for more than 400 business 
software programs.  Digital also offers remote support via modem for 
quick problem resolution.

     The company also has signed agreements with Alaska Computer; 
Brandsmart; Computer Discount Warehouse; Elek-Tek; Fry's 
Electronics; J&R Computer; K's Merchandise; Lechmere; R.C. Willey; 
Rockwell and State Street Discount.  The Starion 300i, 500i, 700i 
and 900i models also are available from these retailers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
