        DIGITAL EXPANDS DISTRIBUTION IN ASIA PACIFIC MARKET,
            ADDS FOURTEEN DISTRIBUTORS IN NINE COUNTRIES


     Company Responds To Growing Worldwide Demand For Reliable,
               Powerful, Multivendor Storage Solutions


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 1, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced expanded availability of its StorageWorks product 
line in the Asia Pacific market, with the addition of fourteen 
resellers and distributors in nine countries.  These new 
distribution agreements will provide distributors and their 
customers with broader purchasing options and greater access to 
Digital's StorageWorks products.

     Digital established the distribution agreements in response to 
the increasing, worldwide need for reliable, powerful, and flexible 
storage solutions that are cost effective in terms of purchase 
price, as well as maintenance and upgrade costs.  By working with 
these new partners, Digital is able to provide end- users its line 
of scalable and modular disk, tape, optical and RAID subsystems, 
which are designed for full compatibility with multivendor 
information systems.

     "The Asia Pacific region is an immense and profitable market 
with organizations clamoring for fault-tolerant storage subsystems," 
stated Ronald Gervenack, worldwide channels marketing manager, 
Digital's Storage Business Unit. "Digital is providing product 
solutions that address this growing need."

     "Developing a strong distribution infrastructure in the Asia 
Pacific region is also an essential component in meeting customer 
demands," Gervenack added. "Digital is working with its new partners 
so users can benefit from StorageWorks products that utilize the 
most advanced controller, media and interconnect technologies, 
combined with ease-of-use features, for 'plug-and- store' usage 
across multivendor networks."

     According to Max Fredericks, general manager of Australasian 
Memory, a distributor located in Castle Hill, Australia, "Until now, 
the rapid changes in I.S. computing environments and the growing 
importance of high-performance, high-availability solutions have not 
been matched by an increased availability of reliable storage 
products.  By adding the StorageWorks line to our product mix, we 
are better positioned to provide our customers with cost effective, 
high performing subsystems that effectively address these critical 
storage needs."

Digital's new distribution partners include:

Australasian Memory Mty Limited, Australia Jungwoo Ace Co. Limited, 
Korea Australasian Memory Int Pte Limited, Singapore LAN 1 Pty 
Limited, Australia Chartered Systems and Networks, Singapore Newtech 
Co. Limited, Japan Dataprep Distribution, Malaysia PT Skill, 
Indonesia Ecoline Automation Systems Corporation, Philippines 
Sunkyong Distribution Limited, Korea i.t. Connxions, Australia   
Syntax Communication Limited, China Itochu Techno-Science 
Corporation, Japan Systex Technology, Hong Kong.

     StorageWorks is a comprehensive family of disk, tape and 
optical storage subsystems, offering modular, competitively-priced, 
industry-standard solutions in customizable desktop, deskside, and 
datacenter enclosures.  StorageWorks products are available on 
multiple operating systems and hardware platforms, including Novell 
and Windows NT environments, plus Digital, Hewlett-Packard, IBM and 
Sun workstations and servers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
