                DIGITAL DISPLAYS POWERFUL LINE-UP OF
                      ALPHA-BASED WORKSTATIONS
           AND LEADING CAD SOLUTIONS AT A/E/C SYSTEMS '95


             AutoCAD Release 13 and MicroStation Modeler
                     Now Available for Alpha/NT


ATLANTA, Georgia -- June 5, 1995, -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
is a major participant in the A/E/C SYSTEMS '95 conference from June 
5 - 8 in the World Congress Center here. The Digital exhibit 
features leading applications for computer-aided design (CAD) 
running on Alpha-based workstations and demonstrates the tremendous 
performance advantages of Alpha systems. 

     At the show, Digital is announcing the availability of two 
leading CAD applications for Alpha-based workstations running the 
Windows NT operating system -- AutoCAD Release 13 from Autodesk, 
Inc., and MicroStation Modeler from Bentley Systems, Inc. 
Graphisoft, Inc. is announcing ArchiCAD, an architectural package. 
(See separate releases). 

     Digital is also announcing the availability of two popular 
graphics boards from ELSA and custom drivers that enable dual-screen 
capability for Alpha workstations and enhance the speed of CAD 
packages.

     At the show, Digital will showcase its full line of 
AlphaStation workstations, including the world's fastest 
workstation, under the theme, "The Alpha advantage for out of this 
world performance." 

     The Digital booth is made up of four main areas -- Design 
Automation, Data Management, Visualization, and an area that 
showcases applications for architecture, engineering, and 
construction (AEC) markets. 

     o 	Design Automation -- In this area, Digital will demonstrate 
        the industry-leading performance of its Alpha-based systems 
        as compared to Intel-based PCs running AutoCAD Release 13, 
        MicroStation Modeler Version 5, and Massteck's MAXEDA 
        software. In addition, Digital will demonstrate 
        Computervision's new DesignPost Drafting software on the 
        Celebris 590 Pentium platform.

     	Digital's AlphaStation workstations provide up to three 
        times the floating point performance of a 90 MHz Intel 
        Pentium processor, as this demonstration proves. That's more 
        than enough processing and graphics performance to handle 
        the most demanding design automation tasks.
     	
     o 	Visualization -- Here Digital will again demonstrate the 
        industry-leading performance of its AlphaStation 
        workstations as compared to a 90 MHz Intel Pentium processor 
        this time running MicroStation Masterpiece software. With 
        MicroStation Masterpiece, architects and engineers can 
        generate and analyze photorealistic still or animated images 
        during the design phase, directly from design data.

     	Digital's AlphaStation workstations offer a significant 
        performance increase as demonstrated at the show, thereby 
        shortening design cycles with fast drawing regeneration, 
        rendering, and 3D animation. 

     o 	Data Management -- This demonstration will feature a Prioris 
        HX dual processor system running Windows NT Server, an 
        AlphaStation 250/266 workstation -- the world's fastest 2D 
        workstation -- and Digital's Celebris 590 Pentium platform 
        all running Autodesk's Data Management software "Autodesk 
        WorkCenter." In addition, Digital will demonstrate 
        Computervision's new Optegra TDM-Lite data management 
        solution on a Windows NT Celebris 590 Pentium platform.

     	Much of an organization's bottom line depends on the 
        effectiveness of its data management. Digital's open systems 
        and superior networking technology enables design engineers 
        to access and share information, from concept through 
        operations, saving time and reducing project lifecycle 
        costs.

     o 	AEC Applications

     	In this area, customers will have the chance to view the 
        high-impact design and drafting capabilities of AutoCAD 
        Release 13. Customers will see how with a streamlined 
        graphical interface, Microsoft OLE (object linking and 
        embedding) support, and AutoCAD R13 they can use Digital's 
        enterprise-wide networking capabilities to share designs 
        with Windows users across an organization.

     	Other leading suppliers of AEC solutions -- including 
        Bentley, Computervision, Graphic Data Systems, Graphisoft, 
        and Environmental Systems Research Institute -- will also 
        showcase their solutions for design automation, solids 
        modeling, mapping, GIS and Infrastructure, plant design, 
     	and visualization in the Digital booth.

     	As demonstrated in this area, anyone involved in planning, 
        design, engineering, construction, or facilities management, 
        can eliminate costly software development with Digital and 
        its business partners. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
