                DIGITAL ANNOUNCES LEADING CAD PACKAGE
                    FOR ALPHASTATION WORKSTATIONS


           AutoCAD Release 13 from Autodesk Now Available
                     Under Windows NT for Alpha


ATLANTA, Georgia -- June 5, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that AutoCAD Release 13 software from Audodesk, 
Inc., is now available for Digital's AlphaStation workstations under 
the Windows NT operating system. AutoCAD Release 13 is the flagship 
product of a family of design automation products from Autodesk--the 
world's largest provider of computer-aided design (CAD) software.

     Alpha is the only RISC platform for AutoCAD Release 13 software 
today in the Microsoft Windows NT environment.  Currently there are 
more than 60 million PC users accustomed to using AutoCAD who can 
now benefit from the outstanding performance of AlphaStation 
workstations.

     "Digital's AlphaStation is the fastest system running AutoCAD 
Release 13 in a Microsoft Windows NT environment," said Philippe 
Ribeyre, vice president of Digital's Workstations Business Segment.  
"Digital's AlphaStation workstations offer unbounded floating point 
performance and industry leading 2D and 3D graphics--especially for 
3D solids modeling and rendering in Windows NT environments. 
AlphaStation workstations with AutoCAD Release 13 software can 
handle the most demanding CAD applications, allowing users to work 
faster and meet tight time-to-market deadlines." 

     "Customers will experience a tremendous speed increase with 
AlphaStation workstations running AutoCAD Release 13 software under 
the Windows NT operating system," said Robert Carr, vice president 
of engineering at Autodesk.

     Bob Noftle, president of independent software developer 
CIMLOGIC says that AutoCAD Release 13 on Alpha-based systems is 
perfect for an engineering environment. The company, which is based 
in Nashua, New Hampshire, has been developing AutoCAD-based 
applications for mechanical design, drafting, and detailing since 
1985. "AutoCAD Release 13 on a workstation as powerful as an Alpha 
system will set a new performance standard," said Noftle. "And 
AutoCAD Release 13 running in the Windows NT environment is a 
benefit to many engineers who are already familiar with the look and 
feel of Windows-based office applications. Digital's systems also 
make it very easy for engineers to share designs and data because 
the systems can be networked together so well. The power of 
Digital's Alpha systems and networking capabilities combined with 
AutoCAD Release 13 will be very attractive to many of our 
customers." 

     Autodesk is the world's leading supplier of computer-aided 
design (CAD) automation software and the fifth-largest PC software 
company.  The company develops, markets, and supports a family of 
design automation and professional multimedia software, and 
component technologies for use on personal computers and 
workstations.  A global company since its founding in 1982, Autodesk 
markets products in 115 countries and 18 languages.  Autodesk shares 
are traded on the Nasdaq National Market under the symbol ACAD.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
