               DIGITAL ANNOUNCES DEC MLS+ RELEASE 3.1

 
       Digital Increases Lead in Enterprise Security Solutions

 
AFCEA Conference, Washington, D.C. --  June 6, 1995 -- Digital 
Equipment Corporation today announced DEC MLS+ version 3.1, the 
latest release of its trusted UNIX(R) operating system.  Based on 
Digital UNIX, the trusted operating system provides a B1 
Compartmented Mode Workstation (CMW) secure windowing and network 
environment for Digital's family of 64-bit Alpha client, 
workstation, server, and network platforms.  The fifth-generation 
trusted release underlines Digital's commitment to address the 
security requirements of the enterprise MIS community. 

     DEC MLS+ 3.1 provides security enhancements to the Digital UNIX 
kernel, and includes security-enhanced versions of the industry 
standard OSF Motif V1.2.2 window manager and the X11 (R5) window 
server.  Enhanced compatibility with mainstream Digital UNIX 
significantly increases the pallet of Commercial-Off-The-Shelf 
(COTS) applications available for Digital's Alpha secure 
environments. 

     Built to enforce Bell-LaPadula mandatory access control - 
wherein users can neither read data that is above their authority 
level nor write data below their level - Digital's Multiple Level 
Secure - MLS  product defines the state-of-the-art in enterprise 
security performance and usability.  

     New features and functionality to version 3.1 include:  support 
for trusted Network Information Services - NIS - full network 
security compliance to Trusted System Interoperability Group - TSIX 
- (RE) 1.0, and configurable window security label display.  
Additionally, the fifth-generation product is based on Digital's 
current UNIX technology - a major contrast to competitors' less 
mature, second and third-generation security offerings, based on 
yesterday's first or second generation UNIX operating system 
offerings.

NIS:  Administration and Management

     Trusted NIS support provides the network administrator with an 
infrastructure to manage multiple trusted hosts across the network 
from a single host.  DEC MLS+ 3.1 allows the administrator to set 
and reset security attributes for multiple network system hosts, 
from assigning accreditation ranges to dictating communications 
protocols.  Furthermore, 3.1's NIS functionality allows the 
administrator to replicate individual and macro security changes 
across all nodes on the network.

TSIX:  The Key to Heterogeneous Deployment

     Full Network Security Compliance to TSIX (RE) 1.0 protocol 
ensures 3.1 relevance within heterogeneous secure environments.  The 
systems strict standards compatibility allows it to be fielded and 
interoperate seamlessly with pre-installed 32-bit security offerings 
from other vendors, such as Sun and Hewlett-Packard, that adhere to 
the protocol.

Configurable Windows Security Labels:  Optimize User Productivity

     An ease-of-use, simplifying, and administrative feature, 3.1 
provides configurable window security label display which optimally 
supports specific user display requirements.  In standard 
implementations, each CMW window on an MLS platform has two labels 
attached - one identifying the sensitivity of the data displayed, 
and the second displaying the clearance of the user viewing data.  
While many organizations require both labels, many others do not.  
The ability to display either one or no labels, allows the 
organization to reduce user confusion and tune the front end to 
optimize productivity.

     In addition to UNIX applications, DEC MLS+ users can access and 
run COTS MS Windows applications on a single platform at distinct 
security levels within separate windows running under Insignia 
SoftWindows.  The operating system also enables organizations to 
utilize COTS office automation products in one window - such as word 
processing, spreadsheet, and database applications - while 
simultaneously running secure applications within other windows.  
Military, diplomatic, and intelligence communities, specifically, in 
addition to other government and commercial organizations, rely 
heavily on information at various levels of sensitivity for daily 
operations.  Having a trusted secure environment is critical for 
such entities.

     The single platform security plurality that DEC MLS+ provides, 
removes the requirements for the development of custom applications 
to run within sophisticated secure environments.  DEC MLS+ reduces 
the entry price for sophisticated secure enterprise computing.  
It will allow organizations that had been forced to run multiple 
applications on numerous classification-specific desktops to 
consolidate operations, reducing hardware and operating system 
expenses and significantly cutting requirements for user training. 

     "While organizations are drawn to client/server for price/
performance, concerns about system compromise, hackers, and data 
integrity degradation have forced those with serious security 
requirements to sit on the sidelines," said Scott Scudamore, UNIX 
Security Marketing Manager at Digital Equipment Corporation.  "As 
some organizations have been precluded from playing, other have 
embraced client/server and been burned by security intrusions that 
they had not fully considered.  DEC MLS+ addresses the three 
principle obstacles to secure environment implementation Q price, 
performance, and usability.  Offering a trusted 64-bit solution, at 
an aggressive price point, with enhanced usability, 3.1 underlines 
Digital's commitment to listen to the customer and to set the 
standard for excellence in the secure enterprise arena."

     Available today through direct Digital Federal Government 
Region, corporate sales channels, government prime contractors, and 
approved resellers and VARS; DEC MLS+ pricing is platform specific.  
Hosted on low to midrange Alpha systems pricing starts at $2,995.  
Hosted on high-end Alpha systems and servers, pricing starts at 
$3,995.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software, and services, together with industry-
focused solutions form business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.  
