                    DIGITAL APPOINTS WILLIAM HAWE
                  TO CORPORATE CONSULTING ENGINEER


      ...Company's Highest Level of Engineering Achievement...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 6, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the promotion of William (Bill) Hawe to corporate 
consulting engineer for Digital's Network Product Business.  The 
business unit develops, manufactures, markets, and sells network 
infrastructure products worldwide.  

     "Bill's promotion to corporate consulting engineer signifies 
that he a valuable corporate resource with broad and significant 
influence within Digital and in the computer industry," said 
Laurence G. Walker, vice president and general manager of Digital's 
Network Product Business.  "Bill provides significant leadership 
across our entire product line including hubs, routers, switches and
network adapter cards.  In addition, he is our leading authority on
networking."

     In his role as corporate consulting engineer, Hawe will 
continue to provide the technical vision, leadership, and support 
necessary to continue to aggressively deliver enVISN (enterprise 
Virtual Intelligent Switched Networks), Digital's network 
architecture and product strategy.

Extensive Contributions to Networking Industry

     Hawe joined Digital's Corporate Research's Group in 1980 and 
was instrumental in many of the very first Ethernet projects when 
Digital, Intel and Xerox joined forces to develop this protocol.  
Later, he was one of the key contributors in the invention of 
Extended Local Area Networks (LANs) and bridges.  He then supplied 
much of the technical leadership necessary for FDDI's later 
adoption, and Digital's preeminent position in this technology. He 
led Digital's Network Architecture Group in the mid-1980s.  

     "Bill has been a positive advocate for many of Digital's new 
product initiatives, and consistently has had the vision to 
recognize important emerging markets," added Walker.  "In essence, 
he has made contributions over the past decade that support much of 
our mainstream networking products today." 

     Hawe serves on a variety of professional boards and committees, 
both inside and outside Digital, and has been an active sponsor of 
research projects at Stanford University, The University of 
California at Berkeley, and at other universities.  He also has 
worked to successfully transfer technologies from the Digital 
Research Group through to the market.  Before joining Digital, Hawe 
was a guest lecturer at the University of Massachusetts.  He holds 
both a master's and a bachelor's degree in Electrical Enginnering 
(MSEE and BSSE). Bill has written more than 25 technical papers and 
holds 20 patents in computer networking.
Digital's Network Product Business

     Digital is leading the way in the networking industry today.  
The company is a major player "converging" hub, switching, and 
routing marketplace, and is the only networking vendor that holds a 
leadership position in all three elements. The company pioneered 
this convergence model for networking in which these technologies 
are deployed on a single integrated platform -- the DEChub 900 
MultiSwitch.  Digital's network architecture and strategy, enVISN, 
builds on this platform to enable customers to create switched 
virtual networks.  

     According to revenue figures from International Data 
Corporation (IDC), Dataquest, and Rising Star Research, Digital 
holds the number three market position in routers, hubs, and LAN 
switching.  In addition, Dataquest figures indicate that Digital 
holds the number two market position in Ethernet switching and FDDI.  
Digital has networked more than 12 million users worldwide. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software, and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
