             DIGITAL TO OFFER 133MHz PENTIUM PROCESSORS
                     ON DESKTOPS AND PC SERVERS


           State-of-the-Art Power for Prioris PC Servers,
               Celebris XL and Venturis Desktop Lines


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 12, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced its plans to incorporate the new 133MHz Pentium 
processor in its Celebris XL 5133 desktop PC and the Prioris HX 5133 
PC server.  Intel announced availability of the 133MHz Pentium 
processor earlier today.  At the same time, Digital also announced 
the new Venturis 5120 in its value line and said that it is shipping 
the Celebris XL 5120 in volume.

     Today's announcement is part of Digital PC's strategy to offer 
a wide range of competitively-priced, feature-rich, easy-to-use 
Pentium PCs and servers.  "We are very aggressive on the Intel 
Pentium power curve," said Howard Elias, vice president, Desktop and 
Mobile Product Lines, for Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  
"With today's announcement, Digital offers one of the broadest lines 
of Pentium PCs available from any supplier."

Celebris XL:  Workstation-Class PCs for Power Users

     Digital is continuing to expand its desktop family by offering 
state-of-the-art 133MHz and 120MHz Pentium processors in the 
Celebris XL power desktop line. Designed for power users, Celebris XL 
systems maximize customer ownership by offering workstation-class 
performance and maximum investment protection at PC prices.  The 
Celebris XL systems are the industry's only PCs to offer an upgrade 
path from 486 to Pentium to P6 and Alpha processors.  The Celebris XL 5120 
with a 120MHz Pentium CPU, 16MB RAM, 256K burst cache, 1GB SCSI hard 
drive, PCI S3 964 graphics card and 3X CD-ROM has a U.S. list price of 
$4,999 and is available in volume today.  The Celebris XL 133MHz Pentium 
processor system, will be available in July, with pricing announced at that 
time.

Prioris HX PC Servers:  Performance and Scalability

     Digital's Prioris HX 5133 is a high-performance, scalable PC 
server available in single- and dual-processor configurations.  The 
addition of the 133MHz Pentium processor expands the 
high-performance options for customers who seek advanced, reliable 
PC servers, but are not ready to move into full-blown, symmetric 
multi-processing.  All the Prioris HX systems are optimized to meet 
customers' needs today and in the future with processor, disk and 
memory scalability as well as a host of fault-tolerance features.  
Pricing and availability of the Prioris HX 5133 will be announced 
this summer.

     Digital currently offers several models of Pentium based PC 
servers, including the Prioris HX 590 and Prioris XLS 590 in single- 
and dual-processor configurations.  The Prioris family's combination 
of Pentium power and high-bandwidth PCI I/O enables the industry's 
most balanced server design to provide customers with maximum 
longevity for their technology investment. 

Feature-Rich Venturis PCs for Enterprise Computing

     Digital offers a full range of Pentium systems for general 
business users.  With the addition of the new Venturis 5120, Digital 
brings the power of the 120MHz processor into the value line.  Last 
month Digital introduced six new PCI-based Venturis Pentium systems 
in its value line.  All of the new systems are designed to optimize 
productivity for enterprise computing users while offering 
exceptional price/performance.  The Venturis Pentium systems also 
offer several ease-of-use features as well as a DMI browser for easy 
network and asset management.  Pricing and availability for the 
Venturis 5120, in both slimline and full-profile models, will be 
announced later this month.

     All Digital PCs are backed by Digital's unmatched three-year 
warranty and worldwide service and support network, including 
one-year on-site.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
