          DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW SOFTWARE FOR MOBILE WORKERS


     Mobilizer TM for Windows TM Provides Comprehensive Solution
                 for Mobile Work Force Productivity


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 12, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced Mobilizer TM for Windows TM, a powerful new software 
tool that increases the efficiency, productivity and effectiveness 
of a mobile work force and allows mobile computer users to work when 
and where it best suits their needs.  Digital plans to begin selling 
Mobilizer software this October through value-added resellers and 
distribution partners and mobile telecommunications carriers to 
businesses and end-users.  The software will enter beta release 
later this month.						    

     Mobilizer for Windows is unique in its ability to integrate 
existing office mail, file and database applications and 'mobilizes' 
them for use on a remote laptop, without any additional programming. 
By providing a client-only software solution, it allows simple 
access to an office network LAN, without the need to be constantly 
connected.  In addition,  Mobilizer for Windows automatically 
manages remote communications for the mobile worker when they need 
to "dial in" to their office network, giving them the flexibility to 
communicate over traditional telephone lines (wired) or advanced 
wireless telecommunications services. 				    

     "Without Mobilizer software, when disconnected from their 
office network - the mobile worker loses the ability to see, access 
and manipulate email, data and database files - decreasing a user's 
ability to access important information," said Allan Jennings, 
General Manager of Digital's Mobile Software Business.  "Mobilizer 
for Windows is the only software product that enhances current 
remote access solutions in one easy-to-use package for the mobile 
worker.  Companies looking to gain a competitive advantage are 
increasingly mobilizing their work forces to move workers closer to 
their customers. Mobilizer software helps these companies enhance 
communications and productivity, and ultimately, increase 
profitability, by allowing mobile workers to access information as 
if they are fully connected to their office LAN."

     "Digital is in an excellent position to be a leading supplier 
of value-added software to the mobile computing market," said Dan 
Merriman, Director, Mobile and Wireless Communications, BIS 
Strategic Decisions.  "By capitalizing on its extensive experience 
in networking technologies and rapidly increasing capabilities in 
personal devices, Digital's focus on end-user mobile software will 
be an important contribution to mobile workers and the industry 
overall."

Mobilizer for Windows V1.0                                          

     Mobilizer for Windows is comprised of four primary components, 
which together constitute a comprehensive, integrated solution. 
File Mobilizer:  Enables transparent data access to LAN network 
drives and enables users to specify files to be mobilized from the 
mobile worker's home network.  Works with all standard PC software, 
such as word processing, spreadsheet and graphics application 
packages.

     E-Mail Connection - Mobilized by Digital:  The popular E-Mail 
Connection TM software by ConnectSoft has been integrated into 
Mobilizer for Windows. Users may download, review and respond to 
mail off-line through one integrated user interface.  E-Mail 
Connection works with most popular email systems including, Lotus R 
cc:Mail TM, Lotus Notes TM Mail, Microsoft Mail R, Novell NetWare R
MHS, Internet Mail, MCI Mail R, America On Line R Mail, CompuServe R 
and Prodigy R.

     Database Mobilizer:  Enables users of remote laptops to cache 
and query, at the record and field level, corporate databases in a 
store and forward manner utilizing ODBC drivers.  Databases 
supported include; MS Access R, Oracle R, Sybase R, Paradox R, dBASE 
IV R and FoxPro R.

     Mobile Communications Manager:  Automates connections over 
wired and wireless communications services so the mobile worker does 
not have to manage connections to a home network. The user's 
passwords, phone card information and private connection information 
are all managed from a password protected lockbox.  In addition, 
connection activities can be scheduled to occur while a user is away 
from the laptop.  Mobilizer also provides troubleshooting and 
management information through an integrated event logger. 

     Digital will also sell its award-winning wireless networking 
stack, RoamAbout Mobile IP, with Mobilizer for Windows, at no 
additional cost.

Distribution and Pricing

     Digital will distribute Mobilizer software through a two-tiered 
distribution strategy that will utilize value-added and vertical 
application resellers focused on providing mobile solutions for 
business and sales professionals.  Mobilizer for Windows offers VARs 
the ease of a PC software tool and the flexibility to easily implement 
solutions.  U.S. list price is $299 for a single user package.

System Requirements

     Mobilizer for Windows supports any Intel based 486 or higher 
class processor with at least 8MB of RAM.  Mobilizer software 
operates on Microsoft Windows V.3.1 or 3.11, and Microsoft Windows 
for Workgroups Release 3.11.					    

     Digital's Mobile Software Business is focused on enabling the 
mobile worker to be more productive, competitive and profitable 
through powerful mobile software solutions.  Information about 
Mobile Software Business and Mobilizer for Windows can be found on 
Digital's World Wide Web home page at www.digital.com/info/mobile.  
For more information on VAR and Channel programs for Mobilizer for 
Windows, send inquiries to mobilizer-info@digital.com.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry- 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
