             DIGITAL ANNOUNCES BackOffice OEM AGREEMENT
                           WITH MICROSOFT


  ...BackOffice family server products to be bundled on AlphaServer
                  systems and Prioris PC servers...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 14, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the signing of an OEM agreement with Microsoft 
Corporation that enables Digital to offer the Microsoft BackOffice 
family of server products on Digital AlphaServer systems and Intel 
based Digital Prioris PC servers. 

     With this addition, Digital is further extending the industry's 
broadest range of server platforms and providing customers with 
enhanced flexibility and choice when deploying Microsoft BackOffice 
client/server solutions.  

     Microsoft BackOffice is a family of client-server applications 
designed to make it easier for companies to improve decision-making 
and streamline business processes.  The Microsoft BackOffice family 
consists of the Microsoft Windows NT Server operating system, 
Microsoft SQL Server, Microsoft SNA Server, Microsoft Systems 
Management Server and Microsoft Mail.  

     Digital and Microsoft have been working together on the 
performance of Microsoft BackOffice, which includes Microsoft SQL 
Server, on Digital AlphaServer systems.  Preliminary work with the 
Digital AlphaServer 2100 5/250 with three Alpha microprocessors 
running Microsoft SQL Server 6.0 has shown an estimated 2,700 
transactions per minute (tpm).  

     "Today's announcement is further proof of Digital's continuing 
commitment to offering the industry's broadest range of leadership 
server platforms for business solutions based on Windows NT," said 
Lucia Quinn, vice president of Digital's Windows NT Business 
Segment.  "Bundling Microsoft BackOffice with Digital AlphaServer 
systems and Intel based Prioris PC servers allows us to provide 
users with a powerful platform for cost-effective client/server 
computing."

     "Digital is a key player in providing Microsoft BackOffice 
solutions to customers.  With today's announcement, Digital provides 
one of the broadest ranges of server platforms to support 
Microsoft's BackOffice family with both Intel based Digital PC 
servers and RISC-based Digital AlphaServers," said Jim Allchin, 
senior vice president, Business Systems Division at Microsoft,  
"Digital's AlphaServers and Intel based PC servers, together with 
Microsoft's BackOffice family of server products provide the 
exceptional scalability that today's business systems require to be 
competitive and cost effective."

     Digital and Microsoft will demonstrate the scalability of 
Microsoft BackOffice featuring Microsoft SQL Server 6.0 on both 
Digital AlphaServers and Intel based Prioris PC servers at PC Expo 
in New York City, June 20-22, 1995. Demonstrations at the Digital 
and Microsoft booths will feature the scalability of Microsoft SQL 
Server 6.0 on Digital AlphaServers and the Prioris HX 590 server, 
recent winner of a PC Magazine Editor's Choice Award.  In addition, 
customer examples of implemented solutions with the Microsoft 
BackOffice family of server products will be shown on both 
platforms.

     A full range of Digital servers with Microsoft BackOffice will 
be available -- from single processor to multi-processor Intel based 
systems and SMP AlphaServer systems.  Digital servers shipped with 
Microsoft BackOffice products can be configured for one to four 
processors.  The following servers will be available from Digital 
and Digital resellers: Prioris XL, Prioris HX, AlphaServer 1000 
4/233, AlphaServer 2000 4/275, AlphaServer 2100 4/275, and 
AlphaServer 2100 5/250.
Worldwide Enterprise Service, Support and Training for Microsoft 
BackOffice

     Digital is a worldwide Microsoft Solution Provider Authorized 
Support Center with 29 support centers worldwide supporting more 
than 450 field locations in more than 100 countries.  Digital has 
more than 20,000 service professionals worldwide including 500 
Microsoft Certified Professionals and more than 5,000 Support 
Professionals trained on Microsoft products.  To assist customers in 
training on the Microsoft BackOffice products, Digital also is a 
Microsoft Solution Provider Authorized Technical Education Center 
and is Microsoft's largest training partner with more than 20,000 
customers trained.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
