                 NEW SYSTEMS, PACKAGES FROM DIGITAL
               BOOST OFFERINGS IN ALL PC PRODUCT LINES


 From Industry's Thinnest, Lightest Portable Multimedia Solution to
   the Company's Most Powerful Multiprocessing PC Servers to Date


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 19, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced significant new products across its entire 
commercial lineup, including new PC server solutions ranging from 
entry-level systems to advanced-performance, symmetric 
multiprocessing (SMP) servers, and new multimedia offerings for 
customers computing both on- and off-the-desk.  The new product 
introductions closely follow the companys recent announcement of 
Pentium enhancements to itscommercial desktop product lines. 
Included in todays announcements are: 

     High-Performance, Highly Reliable Prioris PC Servers 

     -  A new family of scalable high-performance SMP application 
        servers that delivers maximum investment longevity in large 
        workgroup environments through the industry's most balanced 
        system design and robust fault-tolerance

     -  New affordable, expandable PC servers designed for small- 
        and medium-sized workgroup applications

     -  The availability of Pentium 75-, 100-, and dual 
        100-megahertz (MHz) processors for its Prioris XL Server 
        platform

     - 	New rackmount solutions for all Prioris PC servers

     Convenient Multimedia Solutions for Mobile and Desktop 
     Product Lines

     -  A unique new HiNote Ultra Mobile Media Module that easily 
        attaches to Digital's widely acclaimed HiNote Ultra 
        notebook, transforming the industry's thinnest, lightest 
        full-function notebook computer into an integrated 
        multimedia solution weighing just six pounds and measuring 
        two-inches high -- thinner and lighter than many 
        non-multimedia notebooks on the market

     -  An easy-to-add, easy-to-use multimedia upgrade option for 
        Digital's Venturis and Celebris commercial desktop products, 
        designed specifically for use in corporate applications


     "We continue to aggressively expand our product portfolio", 
said Bernhard Auer, vice president and general manager of Digital's 
Personal Computer Business Unit.  "From notebooks to networks, 
today's announcement reflects our ability to consistently deliver to 
our customers a complete range of computing solutions that maintain 
our leadership position in design innovation and technological 
excellence across the mobile, server and desktop markets."

NEW PC SERVERS OFFER INVESTMENT LONGEVITY

     Building on Digital's heritage of technical excellence and 
innovation in systems and networking, Digital PC continues to 
enhance its industry-leading family of Prioris PC Servers.  The new 
Prioris HX 5100 MP server is a high-performance application server 
that achieves the industry's most balanced system design by matching 
Pentium power with the greatest number of high-bandwidth PCI slots 
(six) of any competitive PC server; a benefit made possible by 
Digital's PCI bridging technology.  

     In addition, the new Prioris PC server offers greater 
full-system expandability and processor scalability -- from 
one-to-four Pentium 100MHz processors in a single cabinet -- than 
any other PC server in its class.  The Prioris HX 5100 MP family is 
also upgradeable to future higher-speed processors.  The new 
high-end Prioris incorporates more internal hot-swappable storage 
bays than comparable servers, for a total internal storage capacity 
of 36 GB.  In addition, the Prioris HX 5100 MP includes several 
fault-tolerance features such as a RAID array disk subsystem with 
seven hot-swap drive bays, standard ECC memory, an optional 
redundant power supply, and four failover fans for maximum system 
cooling.   The Prioris HX 5100 MP server family will be available in 
July.  The Prioris HX 5100 MP base system list prices range from 
U.S. $10,399 for a single processor system to $30,299 for a four-
processor SMP configuration.

     The company also introduced the Prioris LX 575 and Prioris LX 
590 -- reliable, expandable and easily managed entry-level PC 
servers designed to ideally suit small- and medium-sized businesses 
as well as remote site and branch office applications when used in 
conjunction with Digital's Remote Server Manager.  The Prioris LX, 
which replaces Digital's Prioris MTE, features more PCI slots than 
its entry-level competition, and a greater number of onboard PCI 
interfaces, such as PCI Enhanced IDE, PCI Fast SCSI-2 and PCI 
Full-Duplex Ethernet to provide an unprecedented price/performance 
ratio for entry-level PC server systems.  The Prioris LX 575 and LX 
590 are available immediately.  

     Suggested list prices for base configuration of the LX 575 and 
LX 590 are U.S. $3,000 and $3,300 respectively. 

     "Given our corporate legacy in networked systems and our 
intimate understanding of the specific requirements of the 
client/server market, Digital PC is uniquely suited to deliver 
products, services and support that ensure customers of a maximum 
return on their information technology investment," said Raymond L. 
Weadock, vice president and general manager of Digital PC's Americas 
Operations.  "Today's product introduction is only the latest proof 
of Digital's commitment to the Intel-based server market and, in the 
near future, we will strengthen our portfolio with further Pentium 
upgrades and enhancements in associated software.  In addition, 
Digital is committed to seizing a leadership position in providing 
clusters of Windows NT-based servers, a technology that Digital 
Equipment Corporation understands better than any personal computer 
company today."

     Digital also introduced today several Pentium processor 
enhancements for its Prioris XL Server family of midrange PC servers 
designed for medium-sized workgroups and print/file sharing 
applications.  The Prioris XL Server is now available in Pentium 
75MHz, Pentium 100MHz and Pentium 100MHz dual-processor 
configurations.  Base models of the Prioris XL Server 575 and 5100 
carry suggested list prices of U.S. $4,479 and $4,849, while the 
Prioris XL Server 5100 DP base configuration is priced at $6,749.  
These new variants of the Prioris XL Server family are available 
immediately.

     Digital PC also introduced a rackmount solution for its full 
family of Prioris PC Servers that, unlike other server rackmount 
solutions, allows any combination of Prioris servers and external 
storage devices to be installed in a rack without modification to 
the systems chassis or wiring.  Digital's rackmount solution offers 
greater flexibility than competing rackmounts by allowing front or 
rear mounting of servers and peripherals.  Digital PC rackmount is 
available immediately for a suggested list price of U.S. $3,155 for 
a 63-inch high unit and $3,329 for an 81-inch high unit.  Additional 
pricing varies with shelving configuration, and cooling and power 
handling options.

     All Digital Prioris PC servers are available through Digital 
resellers and distributors.

INNOVATIVE PORTABLE DESIGN FEATURES MODULAR MOBILITY

     Digital's new Mobile Media Module sets the new standard for 
portability in multimedia computing by delivering the smallest and 
lightest solution in its class -- less than half the size and weight 
of popular multimedia notebooks.  The innovative design of the 
module revolutionizes notebook computing by providing industry-
leading portability for multimedia applications as well as modular 
mobility to meet the changing needs of mobile professionals.

     For example, when attached to the Digital HiNote Ultra 
notebook, the sleek Mobile Media Module adds less than one inch in 
height and merely two pounds of weight to the compact four-pound 
computer -- without sacrificing speed, power or storage capacity.  
It attaches easily to the bottom of the HiNote Ultra in a similar 
fashion to the innovative zero-footprint floppy disk/PC Card module 
that fits into the open space below the notebook and next to its 
flip-down battery.  When multimedia capabilities aren't required, 
the user simply detaches the Mobile Media Module from the HiNote 
Ultra, returning the HiNote Ultra to its industry-leading slim, 
lightweight form factor.

     "Distinguishing our HiNote Ultra Mobile Media solution from the 
competition is like comparing the Concorde to the Spruce Goose -- 
sleek, light and fast versus bulky, heavy and bound by gravity," 
said Weadock.  "Just as we set the standard for smaller, 
full-function notebooks with our HiNote Ultra product line last 
fall, once again we've taken the lead in technical innovation for 
mobile computing by introducing a whole new dimension to multimedia 
portability."

     The company also announced today two new models to its HiNote 
Ultra notebook family that include 528MB hard drives, currently the 
largest capacity hard drive available for systems in this category.  
Based on the IntelDX4 75MHz processor and dual-scan STN or 
active-matrix TFT displays, respectively, the HiNote Ultra CS475 and 
CT475 models with 528MB hard drives are priced at U.S. $3,879 and 
$4,999.  A 528MB hard drive factory upgrade option is also available 
for existing HiNote Ultra customers and is priced at $799.  
Digital's new HiNote Ultra Mobile Media Module will begin shipping 
in the U.S. during July and is priced at $899.

CONVENIENT MULTIMEDIA FOR THE CORPORATE DESKTOP

     Recognizing that multimedia requirements within a business 
environment are different from those of home office users, Digital 
is now offering a multimedia upgrade package for its commercial 
desktop computers that is designed and priced to meet the specific 
needs of business-based multimedia applications.  The easy-to-use 
package includes a quad-speed CD-ROM drive, a high-end Ensonic 
Wavetable Sound Card, Labtec speakers, a microphone, and Astound! 
software for the creation and support of dynamic multimedia 
presentations that incorporate full-motion video and stereo audio 
segments.

     This flexible multimedia solution can be factory installed or 
purchased as an easy-to-add upgrade kit for any of Digital's 
Venturis and Celebris desktop PC systems.   The multimedia upgrade 
kit is available immediately and is list priced at U.S. $529.  The 
company also stated that it will continue to evaluate offerings for 
its commercial desktop products that increase customer ease of use 
for multimedia applications such as video conferencing, integrated 
sound and networking.

     Last week, Digital expanded the power range of its popular 
desktop lines with the addition of 120MHz and 133MHz Pentium 
processors.  Designed for the general business user is the new 
Venturis 5120; and for power users, Digital now offers the Celebris 
XL 5120 and Celebris XL 5133.

     All Digital PC systems are available through Digital resellers 
and distributors and are backed by the company's limited three-year 
warranty and worldwide service and support network.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in todays global marketplace.
