              DIGITAL CRUISES TO PC EXPO IN A FLEET OF
               "VEHICLES FOR THE INFORMATION HIGHWAY"
         NEW PC SERVERS, MULTIMEDIA NOTEBOOKS, DESKTOPS AND
    INTERNET-READY ALPHASERVER SYSTEMS HIGHLIGHT NEW YORK DISPLAY


NEW YORK, NY -- June 20, 1995 -- Under the watchful gaze of three 
classic American sportscars strategically located around its PC Expo 
booth #3534, Digital Equipment Corporation is showing and 
demonstrating a host of new systems, software, and services, each 
designed to ease the path of individuals and businesses worldwide 
along the ever changing Information Highway.  Included in the 
Digital PC booth at this year's event are the industry's smallest 
and lightest full-function multimedia notebook computer, powerful 
and robust PC servers, an array of leading-edge Pentium desktop 
systems, and a host of Alpha and Internet products and services.

     Software to be demonstrated in the Digital booth -- for both 
business and entertainment -- includes a suite of Internet tools and 
utilities for electronic commerce, information distribution, 
workgroup collaboration, and improved security.  For retailers with 
an eye on the cutting-edge, an interactive video kiosk system, now 
deployed at selected Best Buy stores, will be on display.  Other 
business software in Digital's booth display includes a new package 
designed to ease communications for mobile computer users, and 
software designed for the financial services industry that enables 
data visualization and analysis.

     A just-released multimedia game, based on TriStar Pictures' 
cyberspace movie "Johnny Mnemonic", is on display and available for 
a hands-on test run.

Look for these brand new products in the Digital PC booth:

     o	The Digital HiNote Mobile Media Module which, when attached 
        to Digital's acclaimed HiNote Ultra notebook computer, 
        brings full multimedia capabilities to mobile PC users in a 
        six-pound, two-inch-high package.
     
     o	New Digital Prioris PC servers, which ideally suit the 
        client/server computing needs of a wide range of workgroups 
        and organizations.

     o	High-performance Digital desktop PCs such as the Digital 
        Celebris XL 5120 and the Digital Celebris XL 5133 that 
        incorporate the latest Pentium technology.

     o	Digital PCs optimized to provide the best performance with 
        Microsoft Windows '95.

     o	Digital Starion PCs loaded with Pentium power and software 
        for the small office and retail consumers.

     o	Digital MOBILIZER software for the traveling professional 
        who requires simple, yet reliable, connectivity between a 
        mobile PC and an office computer.			    

     o	New Internet firewall products and services for improved 
        online security.

     The Digital booth also features the company's latest laser and 
color printers as well as AlphaServer and AlphaStation systems with 
the power of 64-bit RISC microprocessors.

     To complement all the computer assets on display, Digital's 
Multivendor Customer Service organization offers a wide range of 
asset management services to help companies manage and control their 
computing costs for both Digital and non-Digital products.  The 
services cover hardware and software maintenance and upgrades, 
support, training, Windows '95 migration programs, and network 
planning and management.  Digital, one of five companies chosen to 
provide Windows '95 support for Microsoft customers, is opening its 
telephone lines to PC Expo attendees so they can try the company's 
Windows '95 support.

     To emphasize Digital PC's reliance on its channel partners, an 
information booth is supplying printed information matching end user 
prospects with resellers in their area.  Prospective resellers can 
also sign up at the show to become Digital PC Registered Resellers.

     Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit offers notebooks, 
desktop/deskside systems, and servers through resellers, 
distributors, systems integrators, and retail outlets.  Digital PC 
has doubled unit shipments each of the past three years and was 
ranked by Dataquest as number 11 in units shipped worldwide in 1994.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
