                DIGITAL HONORS FIVE CITY YEAR ALUMNI
            WITH LEADERSHIP AWARDS AT NATIONAL CONFERENCE


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 15, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
presented leadership awards from the company to five City Year 
program alumni last night at City Year's national conference in 
Columbus, Ohio.

     Digital, one of two national founding sponsors of City Year, 
instituted the Digital Equipment Corporation Leadership Awards this 
year to honor corps member alumni who have continued their 
dedication to community service, maintained a commitment to 
excellence and provided an inspiration to others through their 
examples. The winners each received one of Digital's highly 
acclaimed HiNote notebook computers and a printer.

     This year's winners are Spencer Blasdale, a native of 
Mattapoisett, Massachusetts, serving City Year in Chicago; Marilyn 
Concepcion, a native of Providence, Rhode Island, serving in 
Providence; Nicole Fyvie, a native of Toronto, Canada, serving in 
Boston; Steve Spaloss, a native of Nashua, New Hampshire, serving in 
San Jose and Andre Thomas, a native of Roxbury, Massachusetts, 
serving in Boston.

     "We are pleased to recognize these five outstanding young 
people with Digital Equipment Corporation Leadership Awards," said 
Ilene B. Jacobs, Digital's vice president and treasurer. "Digital 
believes in investing in the future through its support of programs 
such as City Year that focus on developing leadership and 
achievement in our children and youth. These five recipients 
exemplify the City Year ideals and they serve as role models for the 
actions that our young people can take toward the betterment of our 
communities." 

     City Year is a nationally recognized community service youth 
corps, headquartered in Boston, that unites young adults ages 17-23 
from diverse cultural, educational and socioeconomic backgrounds for 
a year of full-time community service.

