                DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION LOCATES
          ITS SOUTHEASTERN REGIONAL HEADQUARTERS OPERATIONS
                         IN ATLANTA, GEORGIA
 

MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 15, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the relocation of its Accounts Business Unit's (ABU) 
Southeastern Region headquarters from Greenbelt, Maryland to its 
facility in Alpharetta, Georgia, a suburb of Atlanta.  At the same 
time, Digital announced the establishment of the Southeastern 
Regional headquarters for its Systems Business Unit (SBU) also to be 
located at its facility in Alpharetta, Georgia. 

     The ABU is the unit of Digital that services the corporation's 
approximately 1,000 largest customers worldwide.  The SBU is the 
unit of Digital that sells the company's workstations, servers, and 
network software. 

     "As an important center of economic activity in the South, 
Atlanta was a logical choice for us to locate our Southeastern 
Region headquarters operations," stated James Mobley, vice president 
of the Southeastern Region for Digital's Accounts Business Unit.

     "Digital's move of these important headquarters further 
reinforces Atlanta's reputation as 'The Technology Forest` and our 
growing computer, telecommunications and high-tech industries," said 
James R. Lientz, Jr., Vice Chair, Economic Development for the Metro 
Atlanta Chamber of Commerce and President of NationsBank of Georgia.  

     "Metro Atlanta is the fastest-growing market in the nation's 
fastest-growing region, and I'm sure that this move will serve 
Digital and its customers well."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry- 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
