PRODUCT NAME:   DECswitch 900 Family


OVERVIEW:

Distributed routing software is a new option for the DECswitch 900
family of departmental switches.  With the routing software, the
DECswitch 900 switch is the first product in the industry to provide
routing between virtual LANs (VLANs) in a hub.  The routing also
controls network access between traditional shared LANs and provides
firewalling between workgroups. 

The DECswitch 900 is a key component of the enVISN architecture,
laying the foundation for designing VLANs and virtual switched
networks.  Within the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch, the DECswitch 900 
module can be used to route traffic between different VLANs which 
are formed under software control with the PORTswitch 900 modules. 

The DECswitch 900 family of departmental switches currently includes
two products: the DECswitch 900EE Ethernet switch and the DECswitch
900EF Ethernet-to-FDDI switch for the backbone.  The DECswitch 900EE
provides six Ethernet ports, supporting full-speed switching between
each of six Ethernet LANs; and the DECswitch 900EF provides seven
ports, supporting full switching capability among six Ethernet LANs
and one FDDI LAN.  The products are available as either DEChub 900
MultiSwitch modules or as standalone switches with the DEChub ONE
docking station. 

Since its introduction, the DECswitch 900 family has offered a level 
2 switching capability designed for high-speed connectivity within a
workgroup.  The DECswitch 900 family provides full spanning tree and
store-and-forward switching. Existing DECswitch 900 level 2 switches
can now be upgraded to include routing via a simple software 
upgrade. 

