                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION

                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:   RouteAbout Access EW
                RouteAbout Access TW


OVERVIEW:

The RouteAbout Access products are branch office routers that 
connect remote offices with Ethernet or Token Ring LANs to a central 
site or backbone network. These multiprotocol routers support the 
bridging and routing of protocols such as TCP/IP, IPX, AppleTalk, 
DECnet Phase IV and DECnet/OSI over a variety of WAN services, 
including leased line (PPP), Frame Relay, X.25, and dial backup. 
(Dial Backup is supported on PPP and Serial Line Protocol serial 
lines over ISDN or Switched 56kbps services, using any V.25bis 
synchronous modem.) 

The RouteAbout Access router comes in two versions: the EW is for 
Ethernet environments, and the  TW is for Token Ring environments. 
Both versions have two T1/E1 serial lines that connect to private 
lines such as leased line or dial backup, or to public networks such 
as X.25 and Frame Relay.  Both routers can be used either standalone 
or within the DEChub family.  The RouteAbout Access EW is a DEChub 
90 module which can also work in the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch.  The 
RouteAbout Access TW is a half-height DEChub 900 module. 

Two software packages are available to customers depending upon 
their environment: a bridging/IP package for IP based networks; and 
a multiprotocol package that adds routing for Novell, IPX, 
AppleTalk, DECnet, and IBM environments. 

    KEY FEATURES:	       BENEFITS:

    Distributed Routing	       The same bridge/router software is 
    			       used on the current and planned 
    			       members of the RouteAbout Access and 
    			       the DECswitch 900. Together, these
                               products provide a complete routing 
    			       solution across the network. Common 
    			       software guarantees interoperability 
    			       and reduces training and management 
    			       costs.

    Hub-based or Standalone    This migration path provides 
    			       investment protection and enables 
    			       cost-effective network growth.  Units 
    			       can be used standalone or in the
                               DEChub. 

    Full Protocol Support      Handles all major protocols in 	    
    			       today's networks.

    Data Link Switching        Consolidates the SNA network onto the 
    (DLSw)                     multiprotocol network, eliminating 
    			       the equipment, transmission and 
    			       management costs of running two 
    			       separate networks.

    Simple Software Package    Two simple packages are available, IP 
    			       or Multiprotocol.  These packages 
    			       provide everything required, 
    			       including software pre-loaded in
                               flash memory for easy installation.

PREREQUISITE HARDWARE:

Appropriate DCE device such as a DSU/CSU, an ISDN terminal adapter, 
or modem. Interface cables are also required for the DCE devices.  

A console terminal is required for initial configuration.

SOFTWARE OPTIONS:

Two routing software option packages are available for the 
RouteAbout access products.

    o Concurrent bridging and IP routing
    o Concurrent bridging and multiprotocol routing of IP, IPX, 
      Appletalk, DECnet/OSI, DECnet IV, RIP, OSPF.

NOTE:  Software is pre-loaded in flash memory.  A backup copy of the 
software is on CD-ROM.  A separate CD-ROM is shipped with the 
on-line documentation and viewers for all major platforms.  

