                  MARKET VISION CORPORATION TO PORT
                  FINANCIAL TRADING APPLICATIONS TO
                     DIGITAL'S ALPHA NT PLATFORM


     ... New trader workstation offers native 32-bit support ...

 
NEW YORK CITY, -- June 28 , 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Market Vision Corporation (a subsidiary of Bridge Information 
Systems, St. Louis, Missouri) today announced the signing of a 
development and marketing agreement under which Market Vision's 
suite of financial trading applications will be offered to customers 
on Digital's Alpha systems running Microsoft's Windows NT.  

     Market Vision's trader workstation product, Global Markets 
Navigator, is currently available for Alpha NT.  Additional Market 
Vision product modules will become available for Alpha NT in the 
third quarter of calendar 1995.

     "The availability of the Market Vision trading system on 
Digital's Alpha platform is excellent news for our customers," said 
Mike Gallup, vice president of Digital's Worldwide Marketing Group. 
"Our agreement with Market Vision demonstrates Digital's commitment 
to the financial services market. Digital is uniquely positioned to 
deliver high performance RISC-based trading applications on Windows 
NT. This capability offers our customers a much broader range of 
application opportunities." 

     "We're seeing a growing demand for NT-based solutions in the 
trading market where speed and reliability are key," stated William 
F. Adiletta, President and Chief Operating Officer of Market Vision. 
"As Digital's Alpha platform offers unequaled performance for 
Windows NT applications, and we are pleased to offer our solution on 
their platform. The combination of Digital's Alpha NT platform and 
Market Vision's middleware services provides customers with a 
superior, cost-effective front office to back office solution". 

     Through joint development efforts and partnership with 
Microsoft, Digital has become a leader in providing comprehensive, 
affordable and powerful Windows NT solutions on both Intel and RISC 
platforms.  "Users benefit by having the same, consistent Windows 
interface they are accustomed to, on top of a powerful system for 
developing and integrating applications," added David E. Berger, 
Director of Strategic Relationships at Market Vision.

     The Market Vision software is used to deliver real-time and 
historic market information to thousands of traders worldwide.  In 
addition to Global Markets Navigator, Market Vision's MV Link 
toolkit will be available for Alpha NT.  MV Link is  a powerful 
environment for real-time messages and transactions that provides a 
suite of information services and distribution tools for versatile 
and high performance distributed information management. The proven 
capabilities of Market Vision's products save customer's development 
time, effort and money.

     Market Vision is an established leader in real-time information 
management and distribution software for the financial community.  
Market Vision software is the backbone to hundreds of financial 
organizations providing sophisticated cooperative information 
sharing from market data to the creation, publication and 
distribution of internally generated proprietary data.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions, from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
