             DIGITAL UNVEILS STORAGE MANAGEMENT PRODUCTS
                          FOR OpenVMS USERS


            Storage Management Tools Enable Customers to
            Significantly Reduce Storage Management Costs


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 24, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today unveiled a range of OpenVMS storage management software 
products for Alpha and VAX customers that provide optimized 
capacity, higher performance, improved user productivity and 
enhanced data security.  By implementing these storage management 
tools, users will not only reduce the costs of physical storage,
they also will save on management and operational expenses, while 
avoiding lengthy backups, lost productivity and the possibility of 
lost data.

     Introduced today are Digital's POLYCENTER HSM V1.1 for OpenVMS, 
POLYCENTER Save Set Manager V1.1 for OpenVMS and POLYCENTER File 
Optimizer V2.1 for OpenVMS.  These tools provide users the most 
robust environment for saving, accessing and managing files.

     "Most customers using Alpha and VAX products are grappling with 
far more data to back up and far less time to save and restore it, 
while also facing the increasing need for high performance, cost-
effective operation and uncompromised data protection," stated Gary 
Gottschalk, director of storage software marketing. "These new products 
provide measurable improvements on the efficiency of enterprise-wide 
information systems.  No competitive solutions exist that provide the 
range of capabilities that Digital Storage Management Software products 
do to meet user requirements."

     According to Bert Hajee, senior advisor at the Dutch Ministry 
of Agriculture, Nature Management and Fisheries, Digital has 
effectively met their data backup and access challenges with its 
software solutions.  "The integration of these new products with the 
OpenVMS operation system is seamless, providing a highly effective 
and performing software management environment.  Our experience with 
POLYCENTER HSM in particular has convinced us of the strength and 
usability of Digital's storage management products."

New StorageWorks Storage Management Solutions POLYCENTER HSM V1.1 for 
OpenVMS VAX

     POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage Manager (HSM) for OpenVMS is a 
layered software product that extends the OpenVMS file system to 
automatically and transparently move data between magnetic disk, 
tape and writeable optical storage media according to file usage 
patterns and user specifications.  By providing tight integration 
with the OpenVMS file system, this HSM tool offers a high degree of
data security, integrity and application performance at the lowest 
price of any OpenVMS HSM product.  POLYCENTER HSM is integrated with 
MDMS, a media management tool that allows the sharing of media 
resources with other applications.  This feature enables users to 
share robotic loaders and automated tape libraries without the 
costly and time-consuming re-writing of software.  POLYCENTER HSM 
V1.1 is priced competitively for both entry-level and high capacity 
solutions.  An entry package capable of managing 20 GB is priced
at $1,500.

POLYCENTER Save Set Manager V1.1 for OpenVMS

     POLYCENTER Save Set Manager allows users to reduce their 
OpenVMS backup time by up to 50 percent without compromising data 
integrity.  Save Set Manager is a layered software product that 
performs save set validation, copying and merging of save sets 
off-line.  The Save Set validate function allows users to verify
the internal consistency of a specified save set off-line rather 
than inside the critical backup window.  Similarly, the Save Set 
copy function allows customers to create multiple copies of backup 
save sets without having to run multiple OpenVMS backups.  The Save 
Set merge function enables users to merge full and incremental save 
sets into a new full, reducing the frequency of full backup 
operations and enabling faster restores.  This storage management 
tool also allows users to move OpenVMS Save Sets archived on 
obsolete and/or aging media to newer tape or disk devices.  Save Set 
Manager Version 1.1 offers full OpenVMS Alpha Version 6.1 and 6.2 
support, as well as OpenVMS VAX Version 6.2 support.  The product 
has an introductory price of $795 per node for both VAX and Alpha 
licenses through June 30, 1995.

POLYCENTER File Optimizer V2.1 for OpenVMS

     POLYCENTER File Optimizer (PFO) for OpenVMS performs automated 
defragmentation and placement of files resulting in both higher 
performance and improved disk utilization.  In particular, PFO 
accesses databases created by DECps or Performance Analyzer tools to 
extract frequently-accessed files, allowing these "hot" files to be 
placed optimally on the disk to increase overall system performance.  

The POLYCENTER File Optimizer V2.1 for OpenVMS features an enhanced 
GUI to ease defragmentation selection criteria, a keyboard mapping
utility, and an enhanced monitor window allowing the PFO to locate 
files according to user-specified criteria.  A new capability allows 
system managers to defragment the INDEX.SYS file, improving access 
times to all files on a disk.  Digital utilizes a tiered price 
structure for the POLYCENTER File Optimizer -- the license price is 
$750 for workgroups, $2,250 for departments and $6,000 for an 
enterprise.

     StorageWorks products for Digital platforms and operating 
environments are available through authorized distributors, from the 
Digital sales force, and through DECdirect and the ESTORE.  For more 
information about Digital's complete line of StorageWorks products, 
call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967).

     The StorageWorks product line is a comprehensive family of 
disk, tape, and optical storage subsystems, offering modular, 
competitively-priced, industry-standard solutions in customizable 
desktop, deskside, departmental, and datacenter enclosures.  
StorageWorks products are available on multiple operating systems 
and hardware platforms, including Digital workstations, systems and 
servers, Novell and Windows NT environments, and Hewlett-Packard,
IBM, and Sun workstations and servers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
