                    DIGITAL NAMES SAVINO FERRALES
                   VICE PRESIDENT, HUMAN RESOURCES


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 24, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the appointment of Savino R. "Sid" Ferrales as vice 
president of Human Resources, reporting to Digital Chairman of the 
Board, President and Chief Executive Officer Robert B. Palmer.  The 
appointment is effective June 1, 1995. 

     Ferrales, 44, replaces Richard M. Farrahar, who earlier this 
year announced his intention to leave the company.  

     As vice president of Human Resources, Ferrales will be 
responsible for managing Digital's personnel policies and 
procedures, benefits, employee relations, employee programs, 
development and learning, compensation and rewards programs, 
workforce diversity, staffing, human resource information systems 
and other worldwide workforce-related issues.  

     "I am extremely pleased to have Sid join our senior management 
team," said Palmer. "As we continue to strengthen our financial 
position and focus our attention on revenue growth, we will also 
make a renewed effort to develop the skills of our workforce and 
will work to bring about a lasting transformation of our company. 
Sid will work with me personally to help achieve this goal. His 
broad experience in human resources management and strength in all 
aspects of employee involvement and motivation will be an asset to 
Digital."

     Ferrales joins Digital from OMC Group -- an organizational and 
management consulting firm located in Austin, Texas -- which he 
founded and for which he served as president. From 1989 to 1994, he 
was vice president of Human Resources at Dell Computer Corporation, 
where he was responsible for all global human resources functions.  

     Before joining Dell, Ferrales held a variety of management 
positions during an 11-year tenure at Motorola, Inc., where he was 
responsible for employee relations, labor relations, policy 
administration, security, safety, health/wellness and training and 
development.  His positions included director, Human Resources, 
Corporate Groups; director, Human Resources, Paging Group; and 
manager, Personnel Operations, Semiconductor Sector. 

     Ferrales began his career in 1972 at the Texas Youth 
Commission, where he spent six years providing consulting in the 
human resources development area. The Texas Commission is a 
state-wide agency responsible for the retention, education and 
rehabilitation of juvenile offenders.  

     A native of Austin, Texas, Ferrales holds a bachelor of arts 
degree in Sociology from Southwest Texas State University and a 
master of arts in Social Rehabilitation from Sam Houston State 
University.  He is a member of the Society for Human Resource 
Management, the American Management Association and the Human 
Resource Planning Society.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
