          DIGITAL'S ALPHA SYSTEMS SELECTED FOR OPERATION OF
             WORLDWIDE SATELLITE COMMUNICATIONS NETWORK


         Digital's 64-bit Alpha Systems To Support Satellite
                 Operations Control Centers (SOCCs)

  
MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 1, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced it has been awarded a $1.5 million contract to 
provide computer equipment that will be used to support one or more 
satellite operations control centers (SOCCs) for the Globalstar 
mobile telecommunications system.  

     Globalstar is a new worldwide satellite telephone system that 
will offer low-cost, high quality telephony and other digital 
telecommunications services such as data transmission, facsimile and 
position location to areas currently underserved or not served by 
existing wireline and cellular telecommunications systems.

     Globalstar service will be delivered through a 48-satellite 
low-earth-orbiting (LEO) constellation that will provide wireless 
telephone service in virtually every populated area of the world 
where Globalstar service is authorized by the local 
telecommunications regulatory authorities.

     The contract was awarded by Loral AeroSys of Seabrook, MD, 
which is the prime contractor for Globalstar's satellite operation 
control centers (SOCCs).

     Digital's 64-bit Alpha computer platform will be used to help 
support the tracking, command, control and telemetry of Globalstar's 
SOCCs.  The SOCCs will control satellite orbit positioning, 
maneuvers and station keeping, and will monitor satellite health and 
status in all subsystems.  The SOCCs will also plan and implement 
satellite life-cycle maintenance procedures, including orbit 
adjustment maneuvers.

     "Telecommunications represents a significant part of Digital's 
overall business," said James Mobley, vice president of Digital's 
Southeastern Region.  "We are excited that Globalstar has selected 
Digital's Alpha technology to play such an important role in 
enhancing cellular and wireline telecommunications services to 
people around the world."

     Globalstar, based in San Jose, California, is a limited 
partnership founded by Loral Corporation of New York City and 
Qualcomm Inc. of San Diego, California.  Globalstar's strategic 
partners and local service operators are among the world's leading 
telecommunications service providers and equipment manufacturers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
